==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|donc}}, variant of {{m|frm|doncques}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|donkes||then}}. Of uncertain and disputed origin. Perhaps an [[apheresis]] of {{m|fro|adonc}}, from {{inh|fr|la||ad-tunc}} (compare {{cog|ro|atunci}}), or a blend of {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|dum||while}} + {{m|la|tum}}, {{m|la|tunc||then}}. Compare also {{cog|it|dunque}} or {{cog|ca|doncs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA|donque}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-donc.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|fr|ɔ̃k}}

===Adverb===
{{fr-adv}}

# [[therefore]], [[consequently]]; [[thus]].
#: {{w|René Descartes}}, 17<sup>th</sup> Century
#:: {{quote|fr|Je pense, '''donc''' je suis.|I think, '''therefore''' I am.}}

